
*[NOTE]: This document is strictly preliminary. It was largely AI-generated and contains errors.

.br

.h1 Livetext User Documentation

Livetext transforms plain text to HTML with powerful formatting, variables, functions, and extensibility.

.h2 Installation

gem install livetext

.h2 Getting Started

.h3 Your First Document

Create a file called hello.lt3:

.h1 Hello World
This is my first Livetext document!

*This is bold text
_This is italic text

.set name=World
Hello, $name!

Process it with:
livetext hello.lt3

.h3 Basic Concepts

Livetext processes text files (.lt3) and converts them to HTML. It supports:
.list
Text formatting with simple markers
Variables for dynamic content
Functions for reusable logic
Dot commands for document control
Mixins for extensibility
.end

.h2 Core Syntax

.h3 Text Formatting

Livetext uses prefix-only markers for text formatting:

*This is bold text
_This is italic text
`This is code
~This is strikethrough

You can combine them: *bold _italic text

Formatting Rules:
.list
Markers must be at the start of a word or after whitespace
Formatting continues until the end of the word or line
You can nest formatting: *bold _italic text
Use \ to escape markers: \*literal asterisk
.end

.h3 Variables

Variables store data and are referenced with $variable syntax.

.h4 Predefined Variables

Predefined variables are always capitalized:
.list
$File - current file being processed
$View - current view or context
$Date - current date
$Time - current time
.end

.h4 Setting Variables

Use the .set command to create variables:

.set name=John
.set count=42
.set title=MyDocument

.h4 Referencing Variables

Reference variables anywhere in your document:

Hello $name, you have $count items.
The title is: $title

.h4 Variable Scope

Variables are global by default. Use instance variables for better organization:

@live.vars.set(:user, "admin")
@live.vars.get(:user)

.h3 Functions

Functions are called with $$function syntax.

.h4 Built-in Functions

Date and Time:
.raw
- $$date - current date (YYYY-MM-DD)
- $$time - current time (HH:MM:SS)
.end

Text Processing:
.raw
- $$reverse - reverse text
- $$pwd - current working directory
.end

Formatting:
.raw
- $$br - line break
- $$link[text|url] - create hyperlink
.end

Math:
.raw
- $$isqrt[number] - integer square root
- $$rand[min max] - random number
.end

.h4 User-defined Functions

Create functions with .func:

.func greet
  return "Hello, $name!"
.end

.func format_title
  return "<h1>#{param}</h1>"
.end

Call them: $$greet and $$format_title:My Title

.h4 Functions with Complex Logic

.func format_list
  items = param.split(",")
  html = "<ul>"
  items.each { |item| html += "<li>#{item.strip}</li>" }
  html += "</ul>"
  return html
.end

.h4 Conditional Functions

.func status
  if param == "ok"
    return "<span style='color: green'>✓ OK</span>"
  else
    return "<span style='color: red'>✗ Error</span>"
  end
.end

.h2 Dot Commands Reference

Dot commands start with . and control document processing.

.h3 Basic Commands

.h4 Headings
.h1 Main Title
.h2 Section Title
.h3 Subsection Title
.h4 Sub-subsection Title
.h5 Level 5 Heading
.h6 Level 6 Heading

.h4 Text Control
.br - line break
.br 3 - multiple line breaks
.para on - enable paragraph mode
.para off - disable paragraph mode

.h4 Variables
.set name=value
.set title=MyDocument

.h3 Function Definition

.h4 Simple Functions
.func function_name
  return "Hello, World!"
.end

.h4 Functions with Parameters
.func greet
  name = param || "World"
  return "Hello, #{name}!"
.end

.h3 Mixins and Imports

.h4 Using Mixins
.comment
.mixin tutorial
.end

Loads and executes the Ruby file plugin/tutorial.rb.

.h4 Using Imports
.comment
.import tutorial
.end

Imports functionality from imports/tutorial.rb.

.h4 Creating Mixins

Create a file plugin/mytools.rb:

.raw
def sort_list(args, data)
  items = data.split("\n").sort
  items.join("\n")
end

def format_table(args, data)
  rows = data.split("\n")
  html = "<table border='1'>"
  rows.each do |row|
    cells = row.split(",")
    html += "<tr>"
    cells.each { |cell| html += "<td>#{cell.strip}</td>" }
    html += "</tr>"
  end
  html += "</table>"
  return html
end
.end

.h3 Control Commands

.h4 Comments
.comment This is a comment
This comment spans multiple lines
.end

.h4 Raw Text
.raw
This text will be output exactly as written
No processing will be applied
.end

.h4 Debug
.debug
This will show debug output
.end

.h2 Advanced Features

.h3 Custom Dot Commands

Create reusable functionality with mixins:

.mixin mytools

Create a mixin file plugin/mytools.rb:

.raw
def sort_list(args, data)
  items = data.split("\n").sort
  items.join("\n")
end

def format_table(args, data)
  rows = data.split("\n")
  html = "<table border='1'>"
  rows.each do |row|
    cells = row.split(",")
    html += "<tr>"
    cells.each { |cell| html += "<td>#{cell.strip}</td>" }
    html += "</tr>"
  end
  html += "</table>"
  return html
end

def calculate(args, data)
  expression = data.strip
  begin
    result = eval(expression)
    return result.to_s
  rescue => e
    return "Error: #{e.message}"
  end
end
.end

.h3 Variable Access in Functions

Functions can access variables through the Livetext instance:

.raw
class Livetext::Functions
  def get_user_info(param)
    user = @live.vars.User || "unknown"
    "User: #{user}"
  end
  
  def format_with_context(param)
    context = @live.vars.Context || "default"
    "<div class='#{context}'>#{param}</div>"
  end
  
  def conditional_content(param)
    if @live.vars.Debug == "true"
      return "<div class='debug'>#{param}</div>"
    else
      return param
    end
  end
end
.end

.h3 Error Handling

Livetext provides graceful error handling:

.list
Missing files: Shows "file not found" error
Invalid syntax: Displays syntax error messages
Function errors: Returns error message in output
Variable errors: Shows "[variable is undefined]"
.end

.h3 Debugging

Use .debug to see what Livetext is processing:

.debug
This will show debug output including:
- Variable values
- Function calls
- Processing steps
.end

.h2 Examples and Tutorials

.h3 Simple Documentation
.h1 API Reference
.set version=1.2.3
.set author=Development Team

This is version $version of the API, maintained by $author.

.func format_code
  return "<pre><code>#{param}</code></pre>"
.end

.func format_method
  return "<h3>#{param}</h3>"
.end

$$format_method:getUser()
$$format_code:function getUser() { return user; }

.h3 Data Table Generation
.set items=apple,banana,cherry,date,elderberry

.h2 Fruit Inventory
.func list_items
  items = param.split(",")
  html = "<table border='1'><tr><th>Item</th><th>Length</th></tr>"
  items.each do |item|
    html += "<tr><td>#{item.strip}</td><td>#{item.strip.length}</td></tr>"
  end
  html += "</table>"
  return html
.end

$$list_items:$items

.h3 Dynamic Content

.set current_date=$$date
.set current_time=$$time

.h2 System Status
.func status_row
  parts = param.split("|")
  status = parts[1] == "ok" ? "✓" : "✗"
  color = parts[1] == "ok" ? "green" : "red"
  return "<tr><td>#{parts[0]}</td><td style='color: #{color}'>#{status} #{parts[1]}</td></tr>"
.end

.raw
<table border="1">
<tr><th>Component</th><th>Status</th></tr>
$$status_row:Database|ok
$$status_row:Web Server|ok
$$status_row:Cache|error
</table>
.end

.h3 Custom Plugin Example

Create plugin/reporting.rb:

.raw
def generate_report(args, data)
  lines = data.split("\n")
  html = "<div class='report'>"
  html += "<h2>Report Generated: #{Time.now.strftime('%Y-%m-%d %H:%M')}</h2>"
  
  lines.each do |line|
    if line.start_with?("ERROR:")
      html += "<div class='error'>#{line}</div>"
    elsif line.start_with?("WARNING:")
      html += "<div class='warning'>#{line}</div>"
    else
      html += "<div class='info'>#{line}</div>"
    end
  end
  
  html += "</div>"
  return html
end

def format_metrics(args, data)
  metrics = data.split(",")
  html = "<div class='metrics'>"
  metrics.each do |metric|
    name, value = metric.split(":")
    html += "<div class='metric'><span class='name'>#{name}</span><span class='value'>#{value}</span></div>"
  end
  html += "</div>"
  return html
end
.end

Use it in your document:

.mixin reporting

.generate_report
INFO: System started
WARNING: High memory usage
ERROR: Database connection failed
INFO: Cache cleared
.end

.format_metrics
CPU:85%,Memory:67%,Disk:23%
.end

.h2 Reference

.h3 Complete Dot Commands List

Document Structure:
.list
.h1 through .h6 - Headings
.br n - Line breaks (n is optional, default 1)
.para on|off - Paragraph mode
.end

Variables:
.list
.set name=value - Set variable
.end

Functions:
.list
.func name - Define function
.end - End function definition
.end

Control:
.list
.comment - Comments
.raw - Raw text
.debug - Debug output
.end

Extensibility:
.list
.mixin name - Load mixin
.import name - Import module
.end

.h3 Complete Functions List

Built-in Functions:
.list
$$date - Current date
$$time - Current time
$$pwd - Current directory
$$reverse[text] - Reverse text
$$isqrt[number] - Integer square root
$$rand[min max] - Random number
$$br[n] - Line breaks
$$link[text|url] - Hyperlink
.end

